\details{
\strong{Operation Priority:}
\code{hmap()} evaluates exactly one operation per call in this priority order:
\code{weight} > \code{retrieve_weight} > \code{add_weight} > \code{get_stat} >
\code{detect_disaggregation_group} > \code{add} > \code{set} > \code{compact} >
\code{prune_data} > \code{sync_data} > \code{resync_data}.
If no operation is requested, it returns the raw hierarchy map attached to \code{tdl}.

\strong{Formula-Based Additions (\code{add}):}
You can now easily define custom re-aggregations using formulas. You may pass a
single formula, or you can provide a vector or named list of formulas. In these
formulas, you can set the left-hand side (LHS) as the new parent series, and
you can specify the existing child series on the right-hand side (RHS).
For example, you may use:
\itemize{
\item \strong{Single Formula:} \code{add = Parent ~ Child1 + Child2}
\item \strong{Vector of Formulas:} \code{add = c(Parent1 ~ C1 + C2, Parent2 ~ C3 + C4)}
\item \strong{Named List:} \code{add = list(custom_layer = Parent ~ C1 + C2)}
